      "unit": "U4",
      "test": "owed by the E2 vt plan"
    }
  ],
  "description": "Snapshot and restore (D21; C4 decision 7): snapshot is answered by snapshot_ready — same request_id — with the engine's opaque snapshot in a following kind-3 blob, carrying through_seq (the commit point the snapshot is by construction, C6) and engine. restore carries a request_id, snapshot_seq, cols and rows plus a kind-3 blob of the snapshot bytes, and is answered by restored with the same request_id. A snapshot taken by another engine version is refused with error snapshot_incompatible and no restored; the core then opens an empty grid, feeds it the worker's replay, and raises the stale flow with cause grid_lost (5.52; C2 decision 10) — vt-grid-lost's fixture. Both refusals and both success paths are shown; the opaque bytes are graded by the U4 worker (owed) and the core's storage by the U2 core (owed).",
  "corpus": [
    "plan.md C4 decision 7",
    "vt-ipc.schema.json snapshot",
    "vt-ipc.schema.json snapshot_ready",
    "vt-ipc.schema.json restore",
    "vt-ipc.schema.json restored"
  ],
  "case": {
    "socket": "vt-control",
